186049415 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186073709 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049415 #edb/ref 1031 "Dividing Unit Fractions by Whole Numbers" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049415 #edb/ref 1033 530 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049415 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "f305b2e8-0949-5442-9a4e-a0e42cc69236" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073486 #edb/ref 1069 "e-14418" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073486 #edb/ref 1071 "What division problem is represented by the model below?\n\n![](images/b2/b2e5fb40e703cb3d93f22fd315852930eaab540445e3f570e8de3dacfdc83e0b.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073486 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4fae5cf1-65c9-5217-89ec-54b40e80f293" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073486 #edb/ref 1074 "We have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{4}\n$$\n\non the left and\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{8}\n$$\n\non the right.\n\n![](images/78/785deacac749a6ed43e5e6a2638677e8ff9e9b58087cb4e471ea85fd50609ce6.png)\n\nThe division operation splits the shaded region on the left into $2$ equal parts. So the shaded part on the left is $2$ times larger than the shaded part on the right.\n\nTherefore, the division problem shown is:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{4} \\div 2 = \\dfrac{1}{8}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073487 #edb/ref 1069 "e-14420" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073487 #edb/ref 1071 "What number is missing from the division problem below?\n\n![](images/cf/cf2500f82f337e5635a5ca9854579e3b883f42cde4598d4324c94364bf998a0d.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073487 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9cd2d717-01de-5319-8759-2990e79d64ad" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073487 #edb/ref 1074 "We have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{3}\n$$\n\non the left and\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{15}\n$$\n\non the right.\n\n![](images/ed/ed5517a9242aed1c5b521ca07772dacbb7c96a73c69d4d9c6214a098742358e2.png)\n\nThe division operation splits the shaded region on the left into $5$ equal parts. So the shaded part on the left is $5$ times larger than the shaded part on the right.\n\nTherefore, the division problem shown is:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{3} \\div {\\color{blue}{5}} = \\dfrac{1}{15}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $\\color{blue}5$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073488 #edb/ref 1069 "e-14423" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073488 #edb/ref 1071 "What picture is missing from the division model below?\n\n![](images/9c/9cc5d672cb3c12ceb7704f5136e9b7ecae61d11a9418acf3b8e1cbb9e8f044f7.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073488 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "62d9f262-e419-5a9d-a5cb-741c34613570" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073488 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that in the model, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{3}\n$$\n\non the left.\n\nSince we need to divide by $\\color{blue}3$, we split the whole into $\\color{blue}3$ equal parts horizontally.\n\n![](images/30/30f9bbc604d35a9a15e1418c0cf80eca87fe4d704287c15fb8de7426eb9e3de9.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{9}\n$$\n\nof the whole.\n\nSo, the missing picture is:\n\n![](images/95/951a4bc0607c53aa0c5ed9cebe664b630acf226a6f9844fd9d1b8e6ae952d0ed.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073489 #edb/ref 1069 "e-14424" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073489 #edb/ref 1071 "Use the model below to calculate $\\dfrac{1}{4} \\div 4$.\n\n![](images/8e/8eccf163bffabb43593188590a1f995544f3d1ac0aebcdd87dce638b230f8165.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073489 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c6e1860a-9fe5-559c-8a19-6ed98335659b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073489 #edb/ref 1074 "Since we need to divide by $\\color{blue}4$, we split the whole into $\\color{blue}4$ equal parts horizontally.\n\n![](images/a3/a34a3fb198ef2ea79f8baf8f0acbdbdc179c6259c614824315d3d96e5ea4e921.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{16}\n$$\n\nof the whole.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{4} \\div 4 = \\dfrac{1}{16}\\,\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073716 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074072 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073716 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074361 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073716 #edb/ref 1039 "Identifying the Division Problem Represented by a Model" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073716 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186073486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073716 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "aabbe3f2-c799-5d31-b5c1-8d21b32afccc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073717 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074070 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073717 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074073 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073717 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074462 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073717 #edb/ref 1039 "Identifying the Missing Divisor in a Division Model" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073717 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186073487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073717 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "91201453-ec4d-55a4-8a7b-eae34fca9f8d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073718 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074011 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073718 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074376 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073718 #edb/ref 1039 "Identifying the Missing Result in a Division Model" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073718 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186073488 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073718 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "7bb96a84-3329-5702-ae45-a7d0ad2a95c6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073719 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074012 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073719 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074075 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073719 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074076 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073719 #edb/ref 1039 "Using a Model to Solve a Division Problem" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073719 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186073489 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073719 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "a903aacb-718a-52f6-8be7-a7043358b7bb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073948 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186074605 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073948 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186074606 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073948 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186074607 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073948 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186074608 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073948 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186074609 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073948 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073948 #edb/ref 1045 "Dividing Unit Fractions by Whole Numbers Using Models" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073948 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186074605 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073948 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048460 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073948 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "84bb85b0-fcbc-5f41-956b-e9fb4753720a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074605 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186074606 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074605 #edb/ref 1061 170369 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074605 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f5584f93-514d-5a2f-bcbb-77e4a6db1fab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074605 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186075052 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074606 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186074607 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074606 #edb/ref 1061 170370 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074606 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d78545b2-12fd-53a7-b39d-42f2a610a91e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074606 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186073716 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074607 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186074608 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074607 #edb/ref 1061 170373 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074607 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "35c4a621-9782-54f8-a831-e096eb3088b1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074607 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186073717 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074608 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186074609 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074608 #edb/ref 1061 170377 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074608 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "128f5715-4d86-5558-ae0e-858cc1b44bab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074608 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186073718 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074609 #edb/ref 1061 170380 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074609 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d81020bf-bfb8-5f39-8279-6ca9dd7e5cc6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074609 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186073719 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186075052 #edb/ref 1064 "Remember that a *unit* fraction is a fraction containing ${\\color{blue}{1}}$ in the numerator. So, for example, the fractions\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\color{blue}{1}}2, \\qquad\\dfrac{\\color{blue}{1}}{12}\n$$\n\nare both unit fractions, whereas\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\color{red}{2}}9, \\qquad \\dfrac{\\color{red}{3}}{5}\n$$\n\nare *not* unit fractions\n\nIn this lesson, we will use models to divide unit fractions by whole numbers.\n\nLet's use a fraction model to find the value of\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2} \\div 2\n$$\n\nWe start with a square model of\n\n$$\n\\dfrac12\n$$\n\nsplit *vertically*.\n\n![](images/cc/ccfe0f457342c456200c98cfc46e63bdc1153698282085164eeafae5c2092c45.png)\n\nTo divide\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nby ${\\color{blue}2}$, we split the above whole into $\\color{blue}2$ equal parts *horizontally*. Then, we remove any shaded parts that are not in the bottom row.\n\n![](images/79/7940073ba05d3136ee1d465530a60bc3624b7aa06fd7484d30797758a28976d7.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{4}\n$$\n\nof the whole.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2} \\div 2 = \\dfrac{1}{4}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186075052 #edb/ref 1065 8924 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186075052 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "5efb47fa-47c0-50c8-9c53-0a64bfc732ea" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186075052 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
